{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Basic Controls Available in ASP.NET"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about basic controls available in ASP.NET."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.  Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions Within Sentences"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <b>questions within sentences</b> to introduce a question in a statement; in other words, we use it to implicitly enquire about something, as we are not asking a direct question."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Now, I wonder what to include in the controls if the teacher asks me to list them. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't know what to focus on specifically for the exam."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we talk about <b>questions within sentences</b>, we talk about statements that are mostly used in conversations. In fact, as we are making an indirect question that is included in a sentence, we do not have to use a question mark at all. Now, these questions have an introductory clause such as:</br></br><i>I wonder\u2026 </br>I don't know\u2026</br> I want to know\u2026</br></i></br>After the introductory clause we have a dependent clause; in this case, we present the question, which can be, for example, <b>what to + verb</b>. Check the following examples: </br></br><i>I don't know <b>what to do</b> to understand this topic. I find technology so confusing.</br>  She wanted to know <b>what to prepare</b> for next class. </br> They are wondering about <b>what to include</b> in the next project. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Common Properties of the Button Control"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "ASP.NET includes some <b>properties</b> that allow a better functionality. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some <b>properties</b> of the button control in ASP.NET that you have to be familiar with. Check the following chart to learn about them: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>PROPERTIES\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>DESCRIPTION\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>Text\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This property is for the text displayed on the button.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>ImageUrl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This property includes the image that shows on the button.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>AlternateText\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If the browser cannot display the image, it would show an alternative text.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>CausesValidation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Checks if the page validation takes place after a user click on the button.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>CommandName\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A string value send to the command event.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>CommandArgument\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A string value send to the command event.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>PostBackUrl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Shows the URL requested after the button has been clicked on.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "button "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area that generates an action after a user clicks on it "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should probably put special attention to check boxes and radio buttons."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hyperlink "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "also called \u2018link', refers to an access point for data or information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll send you a document that contains some hyperlinks with that information."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mask "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to protect something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In MultiLine, the password masks the characters that are entered."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wrap "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cover something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Another example is Wrap, which determines if the text wraps a multi-line text box."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "width "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the size of something from one side to the other "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can also mention Columns, which determine the width of the text box in characters."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "uncheck "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to remove a checkmark or not checking something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to know that there are check boxes that can be checked or unchecked and that the radio buttons are those that show a group of options for the user to select."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about Basic Controls Available in ASP.net. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a post with the main characteristics of Basic Controls Available in ASP.net. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your partners the post you created."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for more information about Basic Controls Available in ASP.net. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a post with the main characteristics of Basic Controls Available in ASP.net. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share with your partners the post you created."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Mandy</b>: Please help me study for my test.  It's about ASP.NET, I know you are an expert. </br>\n<b>Nick</b>: Sure. However, I don't know where to start. The topic of ASP.NET is very broad\u2026</br>\n<b>Mandy</b>: It's about text box controls in ASP.NET.</br>\n<b>Nick</b>:  Oh, that's easy! Text box controls are used to receive input from a user. Plus, they are designed to accept one or more lines of text, although that depends on the settings. All in all, text boxes are related to labels, and they are in charge of displaying the text.</br>"}, {"time": "40000", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Mandy</b>: Now, I wonder what to include in the controls if the teacher asks me to list them. </br>\n<b>Nick</b>: Don't worry, some of them are TextMode, which includes a default type called SingleLine and another one called MultiLine. In MultiLine, the password masks the characters that are entered. Another example is Wrap, which determines if the text wraps a multi-line text box. You can also mention Columns, which determine the width of the text box in characters. </br>\n<b>Mandy</b>: I don't know what to focus on specifically for the exam. </br>\n<b>Nick</b>: You should probably put special attention to check boxes and radio buttons. They are linked to ASP.NET too. You need to know that there are check boxes that can be checked or unchecked, and that the radio buttons are those that show a group of options for the user to select. </br>"}, {"time": "101000", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Mandy</b>: Got it! Now, I wonder how to memorize all the list controls in ASP.NET. Do you know any strategy I could use?</br>\n<b>Nick</b>: Of course, read and get involved with them. You have to remember that ASP.NET has control lists such as drop-down, list box, radio button, check box and bulleted. These lists allow users to select items from a series of options. Furthermore, they are loaded by using a code or a tool called ListItemCollection editor.  I'll send you a document that contains some hyperlinks with that information. </br>\n<b>Mandy</b>: I wouldn't know what to do without you. Thank you!</br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n6le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n6le01ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [], "type": "static", "_data": [], "id": 2, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about text box controls. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can exchange ideas about check boxes and radio buttons. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe list controls in ASP.NET."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What button controls do you think exist for ASP.NET?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is the user's input important in ASP.NET? Share your ideas."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Boxes and Buttons in ASP.NET"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "c